  |                                        ^^^^^^
spec/error_monad_tie.kex:11:3: [KEXET-0518]: Error, after `let x = ....tie` on a `[Integer]`, the block runs once per value and answers what `flatMap` joins: a `[Integer]` again, but it ends in a `Integer`
   |
11 |   let x = xs.tie
   |   ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
spec/error_monad_tie.kex:12:7: [KEXET-0127]: Error, `plain` declared to return [Integer] but body returns Integer
   |
10 | let plain(xs: [Integer]) -> [Integer] do
   |                             --------- expected because of this return type
  ...
12 |   x + 1
   |   ^^^^^ this has type Integer
spec/error_monad_tie.kex:17:3: [KEXET-0519]: Error, `return` after `let x = ....tie` on a `[Integer]` would leave only the step it runs in, not the function: end the block with its value instead
   |
17 |   return [] if x == 0
   |   ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
spec/error_monad_tie.kex:22:16: [KEXET-0520]: Error, `.tie` takes a value out of a Monad (a list, an Optional, a Result, ...), and a `Integer` is not one
   |
22 |   let x = n.tie
   |           ^^^^^
spec/error_monad_tie.kex:27:17: [KEXET-0409]: Error, `.try` expects Result or Optional, got [Integer]
   |
27 |   let x = xs.try
   |           ^^^^^^
spec/error_monad_tie.kex:27:17: [KEXET-0143]: Error, `.try` can fail, and `failing` returns [Integer], which cannot hold the failure: return a Result or an Optional, or handle it with `trying` or a `rescue`
   |
27 |   let x = xs.try
   |           ^^^^^^
